#: ../../../gpu_configuration.rst:200
msgid "This is in combination with the following compiler definition:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu_configuration.rst:202
msgid ""
"packages:\n"
"  llvm-amdgpu:\n"
"    buildable: false\n"
"    externals:\n"
"    - spec: llvm-amdgpu@10.1\n"
"      prefix: /opt/rocm/core-10.1/lib/llvm\n"
"      extra_attributes:\n"
"        compilers:\n"
"          c: /opt/rocm/core-10.1/lib/llvm/bin/amdclang\n"
"          cxx: /opt/rocm/core-10.1/lib/llvm/bin/amdclang++\n"
"          fortran: /opt/rocm/core-10.1/lib/llvm/bin/amdflang"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu_configuration.rst:216
msgid "This includes the following considerations:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu_configuration.rst:218
msgid ""
"Each of the listed externals specifies ``buildable: false`` to force Spack "
"to use only the externals we defined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu_configuration.rst:219
msgid ""
"``spack external find`` can automatically locate some of the ``hip``/"
"``rocm`` packages, but not all of them, and furthermore not in a manner that "
"guarantees a complementary set if multiple ROCm installations are available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu_configuration.rst:220
msgid ""
"The ``prefix`` is the same for several components, but note that others "
"require listing one of the subdirectories as a prefix."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu_configuration.rst:223
msgid "Using an External CUDA Installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu_configuration.rst:225
msgid "CUDA is split into fewer components and is simpler to specify:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu_configuration.rst:227
msgid ""
"packages:\n"
"  all:\n"
"    variants:\n"
"    - cuda_arch=70\n"
"  cuda:\n"
"    buildable: false\n"
"    externals:\n"
"    - spec: cuda@11.0.2\n"
"      prefix: /opt/cuda/cuda-11.0.2/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu_configuration.rst:239
msgid "where ``/opt/cuda/cuda-11.0.2/lib/`` contains ``libcudart.so``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu_configuration.rst:244
msgid "Using an External OpenGL API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu_configuration.rst:245
msgid ""
"Depending on whether we have a graphics card or not, we may choose to use "
"OSMesa or GLX to implement the OpenGL API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu_configuration.rst:247
msgid ""
"If a graphics card is unavailable, OSMesa is recommended and can typically "
"be built with Spack. However, if we prefer to utilize the system GLX "
"tailored to our graphics card, we need to declare it as an external. Here's "
"how to do it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu_configuration.rst:252
msgid ""
"packages:\n"
"  libglx:\n"
"    require: [opengl]\n"
"  opengl:\n"
"    buildable: false\n"
"    externals:\n"
"    - prefix: /usr/\n"
"      spec: opengl@4.6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu_configuration.rst:263
msgid ""
"Note that the prefix has to be the root of both the libraries and the "
"headers (e.g., ``/usr``), not the path to the ``lib`` directory. To know "
"which spec for OpenGL is available, use ``cd /usr/include/GL && grep -Ri "
"gl_version``."
msgstr ""
